From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Airoha Team <airoha@airoha.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: allow internal phy-mode on WAN GDM for xPON

On AN7552/AN7563 the GPON MAC sits behind GDM2 inside the SoC.
The PON SerDes is driven by the xPON PHY driver, so there is no PCS
to attach and no external PHY. Accept phy-mode = "internal" with a
fixed-link on GDM ports other than GDM1 and skip the PCS lookup.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3925,6 +3925,17 @@ static int airoha_setup_phylink(struct n
 
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL,
 			  config->supported_interfaces);
+	} else if (phy_mode == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL) {
+		/*
+		 * A WAN GDM wired to the on-chip xPON MAC has neither a PCS
+		 * nor an external PHY: the link is described with fixed-link
+		 * and the xPON client driver reports the carrier.
+		 */
+		config->mac_capabilities = MAC_ASYM_PAUSE | MAC_SYM_PAUSE |
+					   MAC_1000FD | MAC_2500FD;
+
+		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL,
+			  config->supported_interfaces);
 	} else {
 		config->mac_capabilities = MAC_ASYM_PAUSE | MAC_SYM_PAUSE |
 					   MAC_10 | MAC_100 | MAC_1000 |
